WEBVTT

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.450
"Episode 23"
"One from an Unending Dream"

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.290
Archbishop.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.200
Our wish will soon come true.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.040
Griff, I'm proud of you.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.290
You are the one who showed me the way.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:12.370
Emerge and save us, O holy beast equal
to God, nearest to the Original Fairy!

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.500
Together with the ideal world.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:30.830
Marlya!

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.120
Are you all right?

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.450
Yeah...

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.450
Thank you, Ver.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.080
Don't mention it. Can you stand?

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.830
They're gone? Ray Dawn and Griff Mercer...

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.250
Who is that guy?

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:55.620
Fairy Minister Marco Bellwood's right-hand man.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.370
But the two of them turned out
to be central figures in the Eins Order.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:03.200
You said they're trying to use
a fairy-possessed fairy organ

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.330
to do something unthinkable?

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:10.200
Yeah. They're trying
to revive the Divine Beast.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.040
It would be even worse
than the War of Unification...

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.660
The city, the empire,
it would get all messed up.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:19.080
It might all be lost entirely!

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.040
I <i>have</i> to stop them!

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.290
Ver.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.700
You run away.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.120
Go somewhere safe.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.870
Leave Rondacia, go far away.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.830
Just me, and leave you behind?

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:37.500
Well, I don't even have a
clue how dangerous it will be.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.950
Marlya.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:45.410
A long time ago, at Suna,
I left you behind and ran off.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:53.250
That was... But you had to,
so I could get away.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:58.290
Even so, I shouldn't have left you
alone when you were so young.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:02.370
I should have stayed with you
and protected you.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:07.080
But at the time, I was scared.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.080
Ver...

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.700
But this time, it's different.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:15.160
I was a slave to vengeance, and you saved me.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:19.250
I won't leave again.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.950
I'll stay with you.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.910
I want to protect you.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:30.330
We're not related by blood,
but you're family to me!

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.120
Same here.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.620
You're all I have. No...

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.040
I have <i>you</i> . And so...

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.080
What's that?!

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.410
Let's go.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.330
The time of salvation has come!

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.830
The ideal world will emerge!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.950
I feel it!

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:21.410
It's enveloping me!

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:25.500
This is the will of the fairies!

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.080
What?

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.500
It's begun.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.160
Eizenkopf!

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.000
It's a meaningless battle!

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.450
Morzneak!

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.330
Battle has meaning in and of itself!

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:25.580
We don't agree on anything!

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.120
But we can still fight!

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:48.160
Ahh, this is great!

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:00.330
If only this could go on for eternity.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.370
There is no eternity.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:09.080
True. Look how the peace you guys
obtained came crashing down.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.120
We'll just have to take it back!

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.160
That's fast!

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:45.330
No eternity... huh?

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:48.620
This moment is enough...

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:57.790
Even if it's covered in mud and blood,
I'll reclaim it any number of times.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.450
Colonel...

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.620
This is the final battlefield.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.660
Lily!

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.330
Open fire!

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.290
Colonel...

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.790
See you...

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:07.830
Dammit!

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:19.700
Director!

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.620
I'm all right. Let's head to the palace!

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:39.450
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:43.500
For the ideal world to emerge.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.250
We respectfully supplicate the--

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:20.910
What do you fight for?

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.200
What do you wish to protect?

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.790
Say it!

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:34.410
After all those sacrifices and all that effort,
we finally saw a time of peace.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:36.950
I fight to protect that!

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.450
Peace, eh?

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:43.790
If we'd been at peace, your wife
and daughter wouldn't have died.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.540
You wouldn't have lost
what was precious to you!

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.410
Don't speak of me!

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.870
Everything should end!

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:03.290
Hope <i>and</i> despair!

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:07.870
I'll put an end to them!

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.910
No way, it won't end!

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.870
That's some crazy strength...

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:19.000
It's not gonna end.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:23.330
You've been hurting since you lost
what was precious to you.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:27.080
It hurts to want to forget, but not be able to.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.120
There won't be any end to your despair.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:38.040
But for those who come to terms
with it and still want to live in peace,

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.830
their hope won't vanish.

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:41.370
It won't end!

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:45.330
It's always people who crush that hope!

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:47.580
We do it ourselves!

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:50.790
You can't forgive anyone.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:54.620
You mean to punish everyone,
including yourself?

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:57.950
If we end it all, we won't
need crime <i>or</i> punishment.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.000
You think so?!

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:07.540
Howl, Red Hood!

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:10.660
What?!

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.250
I'll cut through it!

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:25.450
Wolf, you still have feelings
for the people you care about.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:27.620
I doubt those feelings will vanish!

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:35.950
Since long ago, humans have been fools,

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:39.370
so we've killed each other
and ruined everything.

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:45.080
But even so, the survivors pass
knowledge on to others.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.580
It will continue on that way.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:53.700
Even if countless people die, and cities
and nations are no more, it won't end!

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.500
No matter what <i>you</i> do, it's not gonna end!

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.080
And besides!

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.330
I... We won't let it end!

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:07.870
Why won't you kill me?

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:12.790
I'm not kind enough.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:39.750
M-Monster!

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.120
Run!

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:51.830
What is this?!

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:55.950
A fairy voice, directly into our minds...

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:00.450
So many thoughts are jumbled together.

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:03.370
It's like it's trying to paint it pitch black.

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:06.700
This is... the Divine Beast's...

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:11.750
Can something like that be stopped?

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:15.080
I don't know. But we have to do something.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:18.040
That we do.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.700
Stand up, Marlya.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.950
Thank you, Ver.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:32.660
If I was alone, I might be
too scared to keep going.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:36.790
Well, if I was alone,
I wouldn't even think to keep going.

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:40.040
Let's go, Ver!

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:45.330
--Move forward!
--Ow!

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:46.870
Don't push! Don't push!

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:48.660
Out of the way! Move it!

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.910
The palace! Make for the palace!

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.450
What's all this?

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.160
Things are totally getting out of hand.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.370
Chima?

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:00.910
Chima!

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:02.250
You're all right!

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.830
Pardon me!

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:07.410
Pardon me. Please let me through!

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:09.660
Damien Albastora...

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:15.080
Are you all right?

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.500
What a day...

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:17.370
You're hurt?

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:20.660
It isn't bad. But listen.

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:23.500
A threat seems to be
approaching from the west.

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:25.750
Threat? The Divine Beast?

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.120
West, huh?

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.000
This is the power of the Divine Beast...

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:46.040
Mt. Panam? Did it come out of there?

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.290
Which means...!

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.830
That's where <i>they</i> must be!

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:59.790
Maybe they know how to stop the Divine Beast!

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.080
Run!

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.080
Run!

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:27.290
I've got a splitting headache!

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.700
This is the Divine Beast's voice?

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:37.250
It's a fairy, too. That's why nobody
but us can hear its true voice!

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:40.410
I don't sense any will, though.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:44.500
Just that it's trying to destroy
and consume everything.

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:54.080
Fairies are supposed
to keep the world in balance.

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:56.500
How could one be bent on destruction?

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.660
Destroying everything...?

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:02.700
If everything was to go away,
in a sense, there would be balance.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.200
It's going to reestablish balance from zero?!

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:08.910
And that's why?!

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:14.250
Destroying everything,
<i>that's</i> the will of the Divine Beast!

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:22.910
Is it headed somewhere?

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:24.910
The palace is that way!

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:27.750
The palace?

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:30.500
I've heard it used to be
that if something happened,

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.910
people would seek refuge in a castle.

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:37.500
The first thing the Divine Beast
wants to destroy is humans?!

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:39.250
So, it's going to the palace?!

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:40.450
Let's hurry.

00:17:57.540 --> 00:18:00.080
Griff Mercer!

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:05.660
Nice view, isn't it?
The ideal world is about to begin.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:08.080
Where has Marco Bellwood gone?!

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:12.450
The archbishop obeyed
his own faith and conscience

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:15.290
and sacrificed himself to the Divine Beast.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.370
What?!

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:20.450
It's what the archbishop
intended to do from the start.

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.750
He was a kinder man than anyone.

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:29.450
Would a kind man... indiscriminately
rob people of their lives?!

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:33.120
I don't think we're going to see eye to eye.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:39.120
You're an ignorant, foolish,
shortsighted, worthless foot soldier.

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:41.120
The ideal world...

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:45.870
The new world that is to
be reborn... won't need you.

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:48.330
Who needs your new world?!

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:54.500
A relic of an old barbaric age
like you probably can't even imagine.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:58.750
I know that someone will have
to clean up after you guys!

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:04.830
You needn't worry.
I will guide the people who survive.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:09.500
That's the sublime task
that's been handed to me!

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.160
A Fairy Weapon?!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:17.750
<i>And</i> a fairy?!

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:38.830
Wolfran Row!

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:41.620
I'm not a man of principle.

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:43.830
You know that, don't you?

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.120
Why are you here?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:51.370
To put an end to the bad dream he's having.

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:07.160
This area is deserted now.

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:08.700
Yeah, but...

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.580
It's just not possible.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:19.540
Is there nothing we can do,
but stand by and watch?

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:28.120
It's too late. We failed
to prevent it, in the end.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.250
Calm down!

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:34.160
The palace is actually <i>more</i> dangerous!

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.450
Open up!

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:35.750
What's the government doing?!

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:35.750
Get outside of Rondacia!

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:38.450
--Let me in!
--Just let us in, already!

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:40.120
Time's going to run out!

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:42.620
Where would we go, besides the palace?!

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:48.040
If we don't protect them, who will?

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:50.700
How do we save this situation?

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:56.040
Hurry!

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:07.830
Big Sis!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:10.160
I can't run anymore!

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.750
Keep going!

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:14.950
You okay?!

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:16.540
Come on, get up!

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.660
Ouch!

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:24.290
My leg hurts! Never mind me, go on and run!

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:26.790
No! We have to stay together!

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.700
Ver!

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:38.700
Where's your mother?
Did you get separated?

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:39.870
Yeah.

00:21:39.870 --> 00:21:41.080
Come with me.

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.540
Okay!

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:44.160
Ver!

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:52.950
This voice...

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:56.660
The Divine Beast isn't
destroying because it wants to?!

00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:58.580
It has no other choice?!

00:21:58.580 --> 00:21:59.660
Marlya!

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:01.370
Go on ahead!

00:22:02.910 --> 00:22:07.000
I'm... going to set the Divine Beast free!

00:23:39.410 --> 00:23:40.910
Aren't you going to keep struggling?

00:23:40.910 --> 00:23:43.750
I believe in you! Believe in me, too!

00:23:43.750 --> 00:23:46.580
If I'm with you, I'm not afraid of anything!

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:48.450
"Next time"
"Freed Sky - Joined Hands"

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:48.450
I can do it! I'll set it free!
